        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ai): defer simple stream API key validation to async IIFE",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a problem where streaming model functions (e.g. `streamSimpleAnthropic`, `streamSimpleGoogle`, `streamSimpleMistral`, etc.) throw synchronous errors when a provider's API key is missing. Because downstream components expect these functions to always return a stream object and yield errors asynchronously, synchronous throws can cause the system to crash or fail before the stream is returned.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplaced direct synchronous throws in `packages/ai/src/providers/` (Anthropic, Google, Mistral, OpenAI Responses) with returning an initialized `AssistantMessageEventStream` that asynchronously emits an error event (via `process.nextTick`) and ends.\n\n## User Impact\n\nPrevents application/gateway crashes when keys are missing. Users/clients now receive clean error events in the UI indicating the missing key instead of experiencing unhandled runtime errors.\n\n## Evidence\n\nPassed 51 tests for Anthropic provider, including:\n`✓ returns stream immediately and emits error event asynchronously when apiKey is missing`\n\nExecution output:\n```\n✓ |unit| packages/ai/src/providers/anthropic.test.ts (51 tests) 88ms\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\n     Tests  51 passed (51)\n```\n\n### Real Behavior Proof\n\nChecked by calling `streamSimpleGoogle` or `streamSimpleAnthropic` without an API key, verifying that it returns a stream object synchronously and yields an async error:\n```json\nReceived asynchronous event: {\n  type: 'error',\n  reason: 'error',\n  error: {\n    role: 'assistant',\n    content: [],\n    api: 'google-generative-ai',\n    provider: 'google-generative-ai',\n    model: 'google/gemini-1.5-flash',\n    stopReason: 'error',\n    errorMessage: 'No API key for provider: google-generative-ai'\n  }\n}\n```\n",
        "branch": "fix/6.1-async-stream-key-throw",
